2.6166C4.35092 22.7683 4.37534 22.9352 4.46749 23.066C4.6275 23.2932 4.94137 23.3476 5.16853 23.1876L12 18.3758L18.8317 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></defs><use clip-path="url(#clip_RatingStar_undefined0small)" href="#path_RatingStar_undefined0small" class="RatingStar__backgroundFill"></use><path class="RatingStar__fill"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/6747279377">March 2, 2026</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">✅ 2 POVs<br />✅ Expansion of the world-building / New setting<br />✅ Politics and scheming<br />✅ Twists and betrayals<br />✅ Forbidden love<br />✅ Some smut<br />✅(🆗) Ahnna felt a little naïve at times<br />🆗 Unlikable secondary characters<br />❗️❗️Cliffhanger<br />❗️❗️Trigger warnings: attempted murder and murder<br />🔥 Spice level : 🌶️🌶️🌶️ / 5<br /><br /><br />I was glad to finally get Ahnna’s book, and while it was not as awesome as I had hoped, I still enjoyed it a lot.<br /><br /><b>The opening is strong and full of action, and the last 10% is full of twists, betrayals, and action, and of course, it ends with a cliffhanger.</b> I was never bored while listening to this book, and I love how the author combined a good amount of action with complex political scheming and a series of twists and turns in the end.<br /><br /><b>Ahnna felt clueless and naïve on many occasions, and she trusted too easily, even though she knew she couldn’t trust anyone because Harendell’s strength is its political scheming.</b> She tried to remain on her guard, but in the end, she let her emotions lead her actions. I think she could have shone more. She is not stupid at all, on the contrary, she is a strong and inspiring woman, very driven and resilient, but overall, she was not as impressive as what we saw of her in the first books.<br /><br />One thing about Ahnna that really, and I mean <i>really</i> annoyed me is that her defining trait seems to be doing the exact opposite of what James tells her, even when he knows what he is talking about and she does not. It was not proof of her independence and strength, it just made her appear immature and too stubborn.<br /><br /><b>The political scheming and lies are at the center of this book, which makes it very intriguing until the very end. </b>Ahnna went into the situation knowing she would be surrounded by politicians and manipulators, reminding herself on many occasions that she couldn’t trust them, yet she ended up listening to them and trusting that they were her allies.<br /><br />The side characters were all unlikable, and even though I know it was on purpose, to show how Ahnna is on her own and cannot rely on anyone, it made it hard to enjoy some parts of the plot. I was hoping for Ahnna to have at least one real ally or one friend at court. Sure, she had Taryn and Bronwyn, but they ended up being rather disappointing and leaving halfway through the book, effectively leaving Ahnna stranded and alone.<br /><br /><b>James is an interesting character and love interest,</b> and he can be dashing and sweep a woman off her feet for sure. That being said, I feel that he was easily manipulated in the end, even though he grew up in Harendell’s court of lies and is very well acquainted with the scheming that Alexandra is capable of. <input type="checkbox" class="spoiler__control" aria-label="The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide." onchange="this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);" id="028a64ac-04b8-4575-aa9d-4b0c8c3a6a1e" /><label aria-hidden="true" class="spoiler" for="028a64ac-04b8-4575-aa9d-4b0c8c3a6a1e">The fact that James just believed that Ahnna would go on a killing spree does make sense because Ahnna did threaten them all when she was angry, but at the same time it is frustrating that he would believe the worst of her so easily when he kept on saying to himself that he knew her so well.</label><br /><br /><b>The forbidden romance was good, and we could feel the sexual tension between Ahnna and James</b>, but at the same time, their relationship didn’t feel as deep and passionate as Lara and Aren’s or Zahrra and Keris’s. I like that they both tried to resist the pull, because of their honor and duty, but at the same time, they seemed to forget all about their promises as soon as they were alone with each other. There is some smut between them, and it does get quite explicit, but besides two times, they do try and manage, for the most part, to keep each other at arm's length.<br /><br />On a side note, Ahnna being angry at Lara is okay, I know it is, but the irrational part of me is pissed at Ahnna for all the hatred she gives Lara and Aren. She hates Aren because he chose Lara even if it was against Ithicana’s best interest, yet she risked the alliance between Ithicana and Herendell because of her feelings for James.<br /><br /><b>The ending was very intense and kept me on the edge of my seat. </b>It was twist after twist after twist, sprinkled with betrayals and lies, and while this couple was not my favorite, I am very eager to read the next book and see what awaits them.<br /><br /><br />1. <a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3092085305" rel="nofollow noopener">The Bridge Kingdom</a> ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐<br />2. <a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3475481063" rel="nofollow noopener">The Traitor Queen</a> ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐<br />3. <a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3614393540" rel="nofollow noopener">The Inadequate Heir</a> ⭐⭐⭐⭐<br />3.5 <a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/4749398051" rel="nofollow noopener">The Calm Before the Storm</a> ⭐⭐⭐⭐<br />4. <a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/4030447672" rel="nofollow noopener">The Endless War</a> ⭐⭐⭐⭐.5<br /><br /><a href="https://www.instagram.com/lucie_v_booklover/" rel="nofollow noopener">Follow me on Instagram</a> 🙂</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/84801697?shelf=audiobooks" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">audiobooks</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/84801697?shelf=fantasy" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">fantasy</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">107 likes</span></button></div><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">2 comments</span></button></div></div><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.4813282,6.41129383 L14.586127,6.97676447 C14.5964421,7.03541935 14.6071117,7.09675198 14.6181364,7.1607667 L14.8551301,8.60363442 L17.440983,8.60363442 C18.1623576,8.60363442 18.8218187,9.01120377 19.1444272,9.65642083 L19.1708204,9.70920723 C19.4523479,10.2722622 19.4523479,10.9350066 19.1708204,11.4980616 L19.118034,11.6036344 L19.1708204,11.7092072 C19.4523479,12.2722622 19.4523479,12.9350066 19.1708204,13.4980616 L1