ery good and the emotions are always so visceral and relatable, but what was this?<br /><br />I did forget that Ahnna was being a little bit of a B in previous books because of Lara, but she was still a really badass character. But where was that here? It started off really promising, but she just turned into an idiot. She ruled for a time and was mostly a commander, so why did she all of a sudden lose all of that intelligence and cunning? Why was she making stupid decisions left and right just so she could say she wasn't doing what she was told to do by everyone.<br /><br />And fuck that ending. Another thing that she could have prevented by not trusting the queen like EVERYONE warned her, but I guess she knows better.<br /><br />And now James is completely off his rocker because he thinks the woman who would do anything to PROTECT her people would assassinate a pair of allied monarchs that would surly bring war to her people.<br /><br />😤😤😤😤😤😤<br /><br />I'm getting real tired of this trope where a character says they're deeply in love with someone but then just completely 180s on that person with no effort to look at what makes sense or why. I obviously understand this situation was highly emotional, but if your woman can be framed and you believe it that easily, then it's not meant to be.<br /><br />And this bonus scene with Bronwyn at the end where James just goes crazy on them too? BOOOOOOOO<br /><br />But I will obviously continue because I need to know what happens but I'm pretty disappointed with this one 😭</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section><div class="Alert Alert--informational">This entire review has been hidden because of spoilers.<div class="Alert__footer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Activate this button to show the hidden review."><span class="Button__labelItem">Show full review</span></button></div></div></div></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul