d of women here was unable to understand any customs. Or make any attempts to fit in even a little to the country she thought she could help rule one day. She knows this is a country that thrives on political schemes but trusts so easily that nobody will possible lie or scheme when it comes to her which makes her seem so naïve. <br />Ahnna decides no matter what she should do the opposite of anything James says. Even when it is to her detriment and he is actually trying to help her. I get that she wants to show how special and independent and not like other girls in Harendell she is but all this does is show her immaturity and inability to reason. There was so much potential between them from the start but it just doesn't get to a point where there is any real communication which is frustrating. <br />There's the inevitable betrayals and splitting up of the love interests to end the book on a sort of cliff hanger. <br />Was well narrated and the book is still enjoyable and I will read the next one. But I had higher hopes and expectations for this one. </span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/5421981?shelf=1-audible-plus" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">1-audible-plus</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/5421981?shelf=2024-release" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">2024-release</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/5421981?shelf=audiobook" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">audiobook</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span> <div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium" aria-label="Show all items in the list"><span class="Button__labelItem">...more</span></but