EK94H1RO"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/ADJY0EK94H1RO\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.0vLaeuJQJc6PKxeF\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/ADJY0EK94H1RO","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/ADJY0EK94H1RO"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.0vLaeuJQJc6PKxeF","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.0vLaeuJQJc6PKxeF"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/84801697?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"audiobooks","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/84801697?shelf=audiobooks"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"fantasy","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/84801697?shelf=fantasy"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/6747279377"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.TJKPtR3KEo46LV5d17g1sA":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.TJKPtR3KEo46LV5d17g1sA","creator":{"__ref":"User:84801697"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1785684238777,"createdAt":1723326066460,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1772461557246,"text":"✅ 2 POVs\u003cbr /\u003e✅ Expansion of the world-building / New setting\u003cbr /\u003e✅ Politics and scheming\u003cbr /\u003e✅ Twists and betrayals\u003cbr /\u003e✅ Forbidden love\u003cbr /\u003e✅ Some smut\u003cbr /\u003e✅(🆗) Ahnna felt a little naïve at times\u003cbr /\u003e🆗 Unlikable secondary characters\u003cbr /\u003e❗️❗️Cliffhanger\u003cbr /\u003e❗️❗️Trigger warnings: attempted murder and murder\u003cbr /\u003e🔥 Spice level : 🌶️🌶️🌶️ / 5\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI was glad to finally get Ahnna’s book, and while it was not as awesome as I had hoped, I still enjoyed it a lot.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eThe opening is strong and full of action, and the last 10% is full of twists, betrayals, and action, and of course, it ends with a cliffhanger.\u003c/b\u003e I was never bored while listening to this book, and I love how the author combined a good amount of action with complex political scheming and a series of twists and turns in the end.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eAhnna felt clueless and naïve on many occasions, and she trusted too easily, even though she knew she couldn’t trust anyone because Harendell’s strength is its political scheming.\u003c/b\u003e She tried to remain on her guard, but in the end, she let her emotions lead her actions. I think she could have shone more. She is not stupid at all, on the contrary, she is a strong and inspiring woman, very driven and resilient, but overall, she was not as impressive as what we saw of her in the first books.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eOne thing about Ahnna that really, and I mean \u003ci\u003ereally\u003c/i\u003e annoyed me is that her defining trait seems to be doing the exact opposite of what James tells her, even when he knows what he is talking about and she does not. It was not proof of her independence and strength, it just made her appear immature and too stubborn.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eThe political scheming and lies are at the center of this book, which makes it very intriguing until the very end. \u003c/b\u003eAhnna went into the situation knowing she would be surrounded by politicians and manipulators, reminding herself on many occasions that she couldn’t trust them, yet she ended up listening to them and trusting that they were her allies.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe side characters were all unlikable, and even though I know it was on purpose, to show how Ahnna is on her own and cannot rely on anyone, it made it hard to enjoy some parts of the plot. I was hoping for Ahnna to have at least one real ally or one friend at court. Sure, she had Taryn and Bronwyn, but they ended up being rather disappointing and leaving halfway through the book, effectively leaving Ahnna stranded and alone.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eJames is an interesting character and love interest,\u003c/b\u003e and he can be dashing and sweep a woman off her feet for sure. That being said, I feel that he was easily manipulated in the end, even though he grew up in Harendell’s court of lies and is very well acquainted with the scheming that Alexandra is capable of. \u003cinput type=\"checkbox\" class=\"spoiler__control\" aria-label=\"The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide.\" onchange=\"this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);\" id=\"028a64ac-04b8-4575-aa9d-4b0c8c3a6a1e\" /\u003e\u003clabel aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"spoiler\" for=\"028a64ac-04b8-4575-aa9d-4b0c8c3a6a1e\"\u003eThe fact that James just believed that Ahnna would go on a killing spree does make sense because Ahnna did threaten them all when she was angry, but at the same time it is frustrating that he would believe the worst of her so easily when he kept on saying to himself that he knew her so well.\u003c/label\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eThe forbidden romance was good, and we could feel the sexual tension between Ahnna and James\u003c/b\u003e, but at the same time, their relationship didn’t feel as deep and passionate as Lara and Aren’s or Zahrra and Keris’s. I like that they both tried to resist the pull, because of their honor and duty, but at the same time, they seemed to forget all about their promises as soon as they were alone with each other. There is some smut between them, and it does get quite explicit, but besides two times, they do try and manage, for the most part, to keep each other at arm's length.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eOn a side note, Ahnna being angry at Lara is okay, I know it is, but the irrational part of me is pissed at Ahnna for all the hatred she gives Lara and Aren. She hates Aren because he chose Lara even if it was against Ithicana’s best interest, yet she risked the alliance between Ithicana and Herendell because of her feelings for James.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eThe ending was very intense and kept me on the edge of my seat. \u003c/b\u003eIt was twist after twist after twist, sprinkled with betrayals and lies, and while this couple was not my favorite, I am very eager to read the next book and see what awaits them.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e1. \u003ca href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3092085305\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"\u003eThe Bridge Kingdom\u003c/a\u003e ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\u003cbr /\u003e2. \u003ca href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3475481063\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"\u003eThe Traitor Queen\u003c/a\u003e ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\u003cbr /\u003e3. \u003ca href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3614393540\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"\u003eThe Inadequate Heir\u003c/a\u003e ⭐⭐⭐⭐\u003cbr /\u003e3.5 \u003ca href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/4749398051\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"\u003eThe Calm Before the Storm\u003c/a\u003e ⭐⭐⭐⭐\u003cbr /\u003e4. \u003ca href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/4030447672\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"\u003eThe Endless War\u003c/a\u003e ⭐⭐⭐⭐.5\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lucie_v_booklover/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"\u003eFollow me on Instagram\u003c/a\u003e 🙂","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/ADJY0EK94H1RO\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.0vLaeuJQJc6PKxeF\"}}"},"likeCount":107,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":2},"User:47514693":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":47514693,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1607749984i/47514693._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":2,"textReviewsCount":85,"n