agging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"enemies-to-lovers","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/109230561?shelf=enemies-to-lovers"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"fantasy","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/109230561?shelf=fantasy"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"feminist-themes","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/109230561?shelf=feminist-themes"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"pretty-covers","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/109230561?shelf=pretty-covers"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/6684878047"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.E9fCPgkpezsRa45hskjAwA":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.E9fCPgkpezsRa45hskjAwA","creator":{"__ref":"User:109230561"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1784966789190,"createdAt":1733802147995,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1754599460468,"text":"I've been following Danielle Jensen since wayyy before she was Tiktok famous. I've always found the romance that she writes to be so tender, and the political worlds she creates so engrossing. However, and I hate to say it, I have found her last two releases (this and A Fate Inked in Blood) incredibly lacklustre. I'm not sure if her writing schedule has been sped up since becoming traditionally published, or what, but I feel like her writing is losing its special touch. This is still a perfectly passable book, but I wanted so much more. The political plot was well thought out, but did not engage me at all. Danielle Jensen managed to find the one political aspect of world building I don't care about, economics, and write a whole book about it. And while Ahnna is a strong character, it was no fun to read about her squabbles with the main characters of previous books, and her romance felt underdeveloped. And finally, while the twist ending was dramatic and high stakes